Z||000000||Loki||10-23-2001||04:46 PM||||Well its official.  December the 18-22 im going to Wyoming to visit my son, who will br 10 months old (will not have seen him in 8 months) Me and the "ex" have talked over e-mail about this and she is allowing me 5 hours a day (better than nothing) 3 in the am 2 in the evening. Ill stay longer if my son latches on. My question is for you all who have children of young age who you have been seperated from for atleast 6 months then getting back in his/her life.<BR>  I know it will be hard and LUke (my son) wont wamr to me right away, but then agian I could get a nice suprise (im hoping). There anything that I need to know or possibly things to do?  I talk to him atleast once a week on the phone so he knows my voice. I was thinking having him on a phone with me on another one while I come into the room so he can associate me with the voice he hears atleast once a week. (I heard him say "mama" for the first time, made this dad proud) Any suggestions or comments?<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/loki_sig.gif">    <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/fieroloki/w4[1].gif"> <BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000001||fierobaby||10-23-2001||06:15 PM||||Loki,<P>good luck I like the phone idea... it would be weird to see omeone you havn't seen in a long time at that age... heck my baby cousin's forget me all the itme and they are almost 4 years old. so my other idea for you is do not come off really *excited?* *happy* *loud?* at first I guess... maybe give him something so he can remember you... go get a nice picture taken of you and get a frame,... I know he's only 10 months but hey he can keep it forever... hope that helped<P>Corinne||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||10-23-2001||06:41 PM||||Expanding on fierobaby's idea...<P>Send him the picture NOW. Let him start connecting the voice on the phone with your face.||||reg||3
Z||000003||AutoXdbdragSE||10-23-2001||11:56 PM||||just a thought, but don't bring him a present.. or at least don't use it as a way to connect.  maybe like take him to do something, and give hime something that is used for that something, so that something will always be yours(i know this is the most vaugue statement ever  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) but i wouldn't like be.. here is a stuffed animal, it's from daddy.. so then the kid will just think of you as a way to get gifts.. at least i think that's what would happen.. but anyway.. good luck i hope you can make your son realize you love him as much as i'm sure you do.||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRiAD||10-23-2001||11:59 PM||||Do speak with (to? at?) him on the phone first...<BR>Don't be too upset if he doesn't attatch right away...if there aren't other males in his life yet, he'll need to get used to having one/you around. <P>Best of luck, man, I know it's tough, but I'll be praying for you. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
